# TARGET ARCHITECTURE: x86_64 | v0.16.4 | on-prem/rhel8
# Enterprise Linux Audit v0.16.4  |  [on-prem/rhel8]
# Tier: tier-1-baseline
# Purpose: failure mode and loginuid integrity
# Source/authority: Applicable STIG audit framework; linux-audit auditctl/audit.rules
# Architecture: x86_64 (b64 native, b32 compatibility); use aarch64/ subprofile for ARM64.
# Release state: engineering candidate; NOT independently certified STIG compliant.


# CAUTION: -f 2 may panic the kernel on serious audit failures. Validate production authorization.
-f 2
--loginuid-immutable
# System-specific auditd.conf, audit service, retention, and forwarding settings are separate.
